$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM α-Chlorobenzhydryl Phenyl Sulfone (7a). Benzhydryl phenyl sulfone (7) was
prepared via the sulfide as reported;24. A mixture of 7 (1.00 g, 3.4
mmol), CCl4 (10 mL), t-BuOH (10 mL), and KOH (4.0 g) was stirred at 3 °C
for 30 min, quantitatively yielding crystalline 7a (1.15 g, 3.4 mmol) as
colorless needles (ethanol). mp 141-141.5 °C. 1H NMR: δ 7.10-7.80 (m).
13C NMR: δ 91.61, 127.85, 127.95, 129.37, 129.91, 131.31, 133.95, 134.70,
136.48.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unexpected differences in the α-halogenation and related reactivity of
sulfones with perhaloalkanes in KOH-t-BuOH
