$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br) 3(3,5-dibromo-2,6-dimethoxyphenyl) 2(BrMeOPh). This
synthesis was carried out in air. Bromine (22 mg, 0.14 mmol) in CDCl3
(0.18 mL of a 0.77 M solution) was added drop-wise with constant stirring
to a pale yellow solution of 1(MeOPh) (24.0 mg, 37.0 μmol) in CDCl3 (∼
0.5 mL). The resulting orange red solution was further stirred for 1.5 h.
The volatiles were then removed in vacuo. Yield 36.7 mg (quantitative).
orange crystalline. 31P {1H} NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): -7.24 (s with
satellites, JPtP = 1570 Hz). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): 7.61 (s, 1H, H4),
4.05 (s, 6H, OCH3), 2.45 (broad multiplet, 12H, CH2CH3), 1.14 (broad app
triplet, 18H, CH2CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM reaction as described by the author
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High Quantum Yield Molecular Bromine Photoelimination from Mononuclear
Platinum(IV) Complexes
