$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,4,7-Tribromo-10-methyltribenzotriquinacene (2) Under a N2 atmosphere,
10-methyltribenzotriquinacene (1; 10.3 g, 35.0 mmol), NBS (20.6 g, 116
mmol), and 75% benzoyl peroxide (1.13 g, 3.50 mmol) were suspended in
CHCl3 (700 mL), and the mixture was refluxed for 2.5 h. The resulting
solution was cooled to r.t., and the volatiles were removed under reduced
pressure. The solid residue was suspended in chilled (ca. 15 °C) MeOH (50
mL), filtered, and washed with chilled MeOH (3 × 50 mL), Tribromide 2 as
an off-white solid; yield: 18.6 g (100%). Mp >330 °C (dec.) [Lit.11a mp
340 °C (dec.)]. FTIR (neat, ATR): 3072, 2986, 1493, 1473, 1460, 1272,
1216, 1178, 832, 749 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.70 (m, 6 H),
7.33 (m, 6 H), 2.33 (s, 3 H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 143.4, 130.5,
125.6, 80.2, 75.1, 36.9. HRMS (DART): m/z [M - Br]+ calcd for C23H15Br2
+: 448.95350; found: 448.95228. Anal. Calcd for C23H15Br3: C, 52.02; H,
2.85. Found: C, 51.74; H, 2.79.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient, Scalable Syntheses of Important Intermediates in
Tribenzotriquinacene Chemistry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beaudoin, Daniel; Rominger, Frank; Mastalerz, Michael
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2015), 47(24), 3846-3848

