$DATUM 1,2-Dibromo-1-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)alkanes 4a,b and
3-Bromo-1-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)alk-1-enes 4c,d; General Procedure. A
soln of 3a-d (10.8 mmol) in n-hexane or pentane (50 mL) was stirred with
Br2 (13 mmol) at r.t. for 12 h. Volatiles were removed and the crude
products were purified by chromatography (silica gel, n-hexane or
pentane) giving pure 4a-d (Schemes 4 and 5).
[1,2-Dibromo-2-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)ethyl]cyclohexane as a colorless
oil, yield 93%. bp 97-99 °C/20 mbar. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.75
(d, J = 14.7 Hz, 1 H, H1), 6.52 (d quint, JHH = 14.7 Hz, JHF = 6.0 Hz, 1
H, H2), 2.00-2.30 (m, 2 H, Cy), 1.56-1.80 (m, 8 H, Cy), 1.29 (m, 1 H,
Cy).13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 143.9 (quint, J = 6.8 Hz, C1), 139.5
(quint d, J = 20.8, 1.5 Hz, C2), 66.1 (Cy), 39.7 (Cy), 25.3 (Cy), 23.2
(Cy). 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 83.0 (9 lines, A-part), 64.0 (dd, J =
150.3, 6.0 Hz, B4-part). MS (EI): m/z (%) = 393 (10) [M - H]+, 395 (15)
[M - H + 2]+, 397 (10) [M - H + 4]+, 127 (100) [SF5], 81 (42) [Br]+, 79
(42) [Br]+. Anal. Calcd for C8H13Br1F5S: C, 24.26; H, 3.31; Br, 40.35; S,
8.10. Found: C, 24.25; H, 3.29; Br, 40.21; S, 8.09.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, the product structure and yield were
corrected by the authors in the erratum published in "Synthesis", 2011,
(5), 827-828
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
