$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)3(3,5-dibromo-2-aminophenyl) 2(BrNPh). This synthesis
was carried out in air. To 26.8 mg (44.4 μmol) of a clear brownish yellow
solution of 1(NPh) in CDCl3 (∼7 mL) was added 1.00 mL of 0.19 M bromine
(190 μmol) with stirring. 31P NMR spectroscopy of the mixture indicated
complete bromination of Pt but incomplete ring bromination. Another 0.18
mL of 0.78 M bromine (140 μmol) in CDCl3 was added drop-wise with
stirring t°Complete the reaction. The volatiles were then removed in
vacuo to give a maroon oily residue. The residue was dissolved in ∼3 mL
of CDCl3 and 0.45 g of NaHCO3 was added. The orange solution was stirred
for 30 min and filtered through diatomaceous earth. It was further dried
in vacuo. yield 40.8 mg (quantitative). reddish orange solid 1(NPh). 31P
{1H} NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): -7.13 (s with satellites, JPtP = 1574 Hz). 1H
NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): 7.89 (dd with satellites, JPtH = 51.28 Hz, JHH =
2.00 Hz, 1H, H6), 7.35 (dd, JHH = 2.00 Hz, 1H, H4), 5.51 (s, 2H, NH2)
2.46-2.32 (symmetric 10 line pattern, J = 3.78 Hz, 12H, CH2CH3), 1.13
(app quintet, J = 7.94 Hz, 18H, CH2CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition (bromine) (stage 1), reaction as described by the
author
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High Quantum Yield Molecular Bromine Photoelimination from Mononuclear
Platinum(IV) Complexes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Raphael Karikachery, Alice; Lee, Han Baek; Masjedi, Mehdi; Ross, Andreas;
Moody, Morgan A.; Cai, Xiaochen; Chui, Megan; Hoff, Carl D.; Sharp, Paul
R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Inorganic Chemistry (2013), 52(7), 4113-4119

