$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Preparation of p-Nitrobenzyl Bromide in SPTRs. The
experiments in SPTR-1 and SPTR-2 were conducted in Bhavnagar, Gujarat,
India (location 21° 46’ N, 72° 11’ E). To conduct the reaction in the
SPTR-1, a single neck RB flask equipped with a magnet was taken, with the
neck sticking out from the glass cover. Ten grams (73 mmol) of PNT
(2-fold excess), 10 mL of water, 16.3 mmol of NaBr and 8.15 mmol of
NaBrO3 (total 24.45 mmol active Br) were added into the flask. The
contents were stirred with the built-in magnetic stirrer and 26 mmol of
KHSO4 was added in lots once the PNT melted. The total reaction time was
around 2.0-2.5 h. The flask was left standing to attain room temperature
and 15-20 mL of water was added whereupon the oily organic mass
solidified. The aqueous layer was drained out and the solid was washed a
couple of times with water. The solid was then ground, dried and
analyzed. The atmospheric pressure, ambient temperature, wind speed and
humidity were measured during the reaction. For the scaled up study in
SPTR-2, 100 g of PNT (730 mmol) was added into a 2-neck flask, followed
by addition of 2:1 NaBr/NaBrO3 solid reagent (245 mmol of active bromine)
and 40 mL of water. After molten conditions were achieved, ∼100 mL of an
aqueous solution containing 36 g of KHSO4 (267 mmol, 1.1 equiv with
respect to active bromine) was added in lots and the reaction conducted
as before. NMR data 1H NMR (CDCl3-500 MHz): δ 8.21-8.23 (2H, d, J=8.5);
7.58-7.6 (2H, d, J=8.5); 4.55 (2H, S). 13C NMR (CDCl3-500 MHz): δ 147.7,
144.8, 129.9 (2C), 124.0 (2C), 31.0 Ѵmax (KBr): 3051, 2840, 2378, 1604,
1534, 1344, 1224, 1099, 1011, 874, 798, 692, 592 cm-1 Melting point
(product of Entry 4, Table 3) Observed: 97-1000 C, Reported: 96-990 C
(Sigma Aldrich electronic database)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, work-up, supercritical CO2 extraction, optimized on
temperature, light source, scalable, optimization study, solar
photothermal reactor used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solar Photothermochemical Reaction and Supercritical CO2 Work up for a
Fully Green Process of Preparation of Pure p-Nitrobenzyl Bromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dinda, Milan; Chakraborty, Supratim; Samanta, Supravat; Bhatt, Chitrangi;
Maiti, Subarna; Roy, Sandip; Kadam, Yogesh; Ghosh, Pushpito K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Environmental Science & Technology (2013), 47(18), 10535-10540

