$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Iodocyclohexane; Typical Procedure. Iodine
(635 mg, 2.5 mmol) and Br2 (80 mg, 25.6 mL, 0.5 mmol) were dissolved in
cyclohexane (20 mL, 185 mmol) and t-BuONa (288 mg, 3 mmol) was added. The
suspension was stirred at 40 °C for 15 h. The mixture was washed with 1%
aq Na2S2O3 (30 mL) and dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed under
reduced pressure and the residue distilled to yield iodocyclohexane 9
(Hal = I). Benzyl Bromide (11; Hal = Br)36, quantitative yield. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.37 (s, 2 H, CH2Br), 7.14-7.28 (m, 5 H, Ar-H). 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 33.7, 128.5, 128.9, 129.9, 137.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct bromination and iodination of non-activated alkanes by hypohalite
reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Montoro, Raul; Wirth, Thomas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2005), (9), 1473-1478

