$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM From cis-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(anthracen-10-yl). Method B. A carbon tetrachloride
(0.3 mL) solution of bromine (1.6 μL, 0.031 mmol) was added dropwise to a
stirred carbon tetrachloride solution (2 mL) of
trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(anthracen-10-yl) (20.7 mg, 0.0300 mmol). The
resulting mixture was stirred for 10 min at room temperature and then the
volatiles were removed in vacuo. The solid residue was washed with cold
hexane and dried in vacuo to give 22.8 mg (99 %) of brown solid. Yellow
crystals for X-ray analysis were obtained by recrystallization from
CH2Cl2/hexane at room temperature. 1H NMR (250 MHz, C6D6): 9.41 (dd, J =
7.5 Hz, J = 1.75 Hz, 2H), 8.78 (dd, J = 7.25 Hz, J = 1.75 Hz 2H),
7.31-7.41 (m, 4H), 1.22-1.38 (m, 12H, CH2CH3), 0.62-0.74 (m, 18H,
CH2CH3). 31P NMR (101 MHz, C6D6): 10.0 (s with satellites, J PtP = 2635
Hz). 13C{1H} NMR (62.9 MHz, C6D6): 152 (s), 138.6 (t with satellites, J
PC = 3.2 Hz, J PtC = 28.3 Hz), 136.3 (s with satellites, J PtC = 96.4
Hz), 131.5 (s with satellites, J PtC = 60 Hz), 127.4 (s), 122.6 (s),
122.4 (s), 117.0 (s), 14.9 (t with satellites, J PC = 17.0 Hz, J PtC =
69.5 Hz, PCH2CH3), 7.85 (s with satellites, J PtC = 22.3 Hz,PCH2CH3).
195Pt NMR (64.5 MHz, CDCl3): -2819.3 (t, J PtP = 2663 Hz). Anal. Calcd
(found) for C26H38Br2P2Pt: C, 40.69 (40.41); H, 4.99 (4.72).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Remarkable Bromination and Blue Emission of 9-Anthracenyl Pt(II)
Complexes
