$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of 2-bromo allyl alcohol (2). Method
A: A mixture of allyl alcohol derivative 1 (1.0 equiv) and pyridinium
bromide perbromide (1.1 equiv) in 1,2-dichloroethane (0.1 M) was stirred
at room temperature for 12-14h. DBU (3.1 equiv) was added to the reaction
mixture at 0 °C and the system was then heated to 60 °C. The reaction was
quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl or 1 M aqueous HCl, and the
reaction mixture was extracted with dichloromethane or chloroform,
concentrated in vacuo, and purified by silica gel column chromatography
to afford 2-bromo allyl alcohol 2. 1-(2-Bromoallyloxy)-2-nitrobenzene
(2b). yellow liquid, yield 91%. IR (neat) 3109, 3078, 2924, 2870, 1635,
1604, 1527, 1489, 1450, 1350 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 7.80-7.91
(m, 1H), 7.49-7.59 (m, 1H), 7.01-7.13 (m, 2H), 6.12-6.17 (m, 1H),
5.68-5.75 (m, 1H), 4.70-4.80 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 150.8
(C), 139.9 (C), 134.1 (CH), 125.7 (CH), 124.7 (C), 121.3 (CH), 118.3
(CH2), 115.0 (CH), 72.2 (CH2); HRMS-ESI [M + Na]+ calcd for C9H8BrNNaO3:
279.9580, found 279.9580.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel One-Pot Method for Chemoselective Bromination and Sequential
Sonogashira Coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kutsumura, Noriki; Niwa, Kentaro; Saito, Takao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(15), 3316-3319

