$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(3, 6, 9-tribromoanthracen-10-yl). A carbon
tetrachloride (0.3 mL) solution of bromine (4.7 μL, 0.091 mmol) was added
dropwise to a stirred carbon tetrachloride solution of
trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(anthracen-10-yl) (20.7 mg, 0.0300 mmol) and silica
gel (2-3 mg). The resulting mixture was stirred for 2 hr at room
temperature. The silica gel was removed by filtration then the volatiles
were removed in vacuo. The solid residue was washed with cold hexane and
dried in vacuo to give 27.4 mg (99 %) of pale yellow solid. Yellow
crystals for X-ray analysis were obtained by recrystallization from
CH2Cl2/hexane at room temperature 1H NMR (250 MHz, C6D6): 9.71 (d with
satellites, J = 2.1 Hz, J PtH = 11.5 Hz, 2H), 8.41 (d with satellites, J
= 9.3 Hz, JPtH = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.38 (dd, J = 9.3 Hz, J = 2.1 Hz, 2H),
1.18-1.30 (m, 12H, CH2CH3), 0.65-0.78 (m, 18H, CH2CH3). 31P NMR (101 MHz,
C6D6): 10.7 (s with satellites, J PtP = 2569 Hz). 13C{1H} NMR (62.9 MHz,
CDCl3): 149.1 (s with satellites, J PC = 9.0 Hz), 138.9 (t with
satellites, J PC = 3.8 Hz, J PtC = 27.7 Hz), 136.9 (s with satellites, J
PtC = 101.4 Hz), 130.4 (s), 129.5 (s), 129.1 (s with satellites, J PtC =
60 Hz), 117.1 (s), 116.7 (s), 14.5 (t with satellites, J PC = 17.1 Hz, J
PtC = 68.9 Hz, PCH2CH3), 7.8 (s with satellites, J PtC = 22.6 Hz,
PCH2CH3). 195Pt NMR (64.5 MHz, CDCl3): -2804.8 (t, J PtP = 2572Hz). Anal.
Calcd (found) for C26H36Br4P2Pt: C, 33.75 (33.38); H, 3.92 (3.59).
