$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Chloro-α -bromoethylbenzene (8) Br2 (56.8 g, 0.356 mol) was added
dropwise to 2 (50.0 g, 0.356 mol) in the presence of
2,2'-azobis(isobutyronitrile) (5.8 mg, 0.0356 mmol) at 50-60 °C for 0.5
h. The solution was heated at 50 °C for additional 0.5 h. After cooling
to r.t., the reaction was quenched with H2O and extracted with CH2Cl2.
The organic layer was separated and concentrated under reduced pressure
to afford pure 811 (from 2). Pale yellow oil, yield 78.0 g, 0.355 mol,
>99%. IR (KBr): ν = 1570, 1480, 1210, 780 cm-1. 1H NMR: δ = 2.02 (3H, d,
J = 6.9 Hz), 5.13 (1H, q, J = 6.9 Hz), 7.26-7.33 (3H, m), 7.43 (1H, s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A practical synthesis of Indanofan via one-pot bromination of
3-chloroethylbenzene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tanaka, Ken; Hosokawa, Akemi; Yoshida, Kenji
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1999), (2), 249-253

