$DATUM Preparation of 1,2-Bis-bromomethyl-3-methoxybenzene (6).
1-Methoxy-2,3-dimethyl-benzene (40 g, 0.29 mol), N-bromo-succinimide
(104.6 g, 0.5877 mol), and 2,2'-azo-bis-isobutyronitrile (2 g, 0.01 mol)
were dissolved in carbon tetrachloride (800 mL). The mixture was heated
to reflux and was allowed to stir overnight. The reaction mixture was
cooled, and the solids were collected by filtration. The filtrate was
then washed with saturated sodium bicarbonate and extracted with
dichloromethane. Combined organic layers were dried over sodium sulfate,
filtered, and concentrated under vacuum. Yield: (86 g, 99%). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 7.23 (t, 1H, J = 8.05 Hz), 6.96 (d, 1H, J = 7.64 Hz), 6.86 (d,
1 H, J = 8.36 Hz), 4.77 (s, 2H), 4.61 (s, 2H), 3.89 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, 2 eq. of NBS used, selective for substitution of Me
groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of an orally efficacious inhibitor of anaplastic lymphoma
kinase
