$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM α-Bromobenzhydryl 4-Methoxyphenyl Sulfone (9b). Reaction of 9 with
CBrCl3. A mixture of 9 (1.69 g, 5 mmol), KOH (4.00 g, 61 mmol), t-BuOH
(30 mL), and CBrCl3 (30 mL) stirred at 25 °C for 30 min provided crystals
of 9b (2.04 g, 98% yield). mp 169.5-170.5 °C (CHCl3). 1H NMR
[CDCl3(CD3)2C=O]: δ 3.78 (s, 3 H), 6.72 (d, J = 9 Hz, 2 H), 7.10-748 (m,
8 H), 7.50-783 (m, 4 H). Anal. Calcd for C20H17BrO3S: C, 57.56; H, 4.11;
Br, 19.15; S, 7.68. Found: C, 57.41; H, 4.12; Br, 19.11; S, 7.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unexpected differences in the α-halogenation and related reactivity of
sulfones with perhaloalkanes in KOH-t-BuOH
