$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(cis-1, 2, 3, 6, 9-pentabromo-1,
2-dihydroanthracen-10-yl). A carbon tetrachloride (0.3 mL) solution of
bromine (30.8 μL, 0.600 mmol) was added dropwise to a stirred carbon
tetrachloride solution (5 mL) of trans-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(Br)(anthracen-10-yl)
(20.7 mg, 0.0300 mmol). The resulting solution was stirred for 5 min at
room temperature then the volatiles were removed in vacuo. The solid
residue was washed with cold hexane and dried in vacuo to give 31.9 mg
(98 %) of pale brown solid 1H NMR (250 MHz, C6D6): 9.55 (d with
satellites, J = 2.1 Hz, JPtH = 12.5 Hz, 1H, H5), 8.60 (d with satellites,
J = 0.8 Hz, J PtH = 12.8 Hz, 1H, H4), 7.98 (d with satellites, J = 9.0
Hz, J PtH = 6.5 Hz,1H, H8), 7.32 (dd, J = 9.0 Hz, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H, H7),
6.24 (d, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H, H1), 5.08 (dd, J = 2.6 Hz, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H, H2),
1.29-1.43 (m, 12H, CH2CH3), 0.70-0.84 (m, 18H, CH2CH3). A COSY spectrum
confirmed coupling between H1 and H2 and between H7 and H8. The
assignment of the cis-1,2 stereochemistry is based on the small vicinal
coupling between H1 and H2.(See: Cakmak, O.; Erenler, R.; Tutar, A.;
Celik, N. J. Org. Chem. 2006, 71, 1795-1801.) 31P NMR (101 MHz, C6D6):
10.4 (s with satellites, J PtP = 2542 Hz). 13C{1H} NMR (75.5 MHz, CCl4):
147.1 (s with satellites, J PtC = 9.1 Hz), 141.7 (s), 137.9 (s), 136.6 (s
with satellites, J PtC = 93.6 Hz), 133.5 (s), 130.6 (s), 129.9 (s), 129.7
(s), 128.9 (s), 121.3 (s), 119.8 (s), 116.6 (s), 53.9 (s), 51.8 (s), 14.6
(t, J CP = 17.4 Hz P1CH2CH3), 14.2 (t, J CP = 16.6 Hz P2CH2CH3), 7.8 (d
with satellites, J CP = 5.3 Hz, J PtC = 28.7 Hz, PCH2CH3). 195Pt NMR
(64.5 MHz, CDCl3): -2782 (t, J PtP = 2600 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
