$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-Bromo-3,4-bis-bromomethyl-2,5-bis-hexyloxybenzene (7d). NBS (9.8 g, 55
mmol) was added in one portion to a solution of 6d (10.1 g, 26.2 mmol) in
CCl4 (150 mL) under argon. A 250W(115-125 V) IR heat lamp was positioned
near the reaction flask to ensure a gentle reflux. After 24 h, the
solution was cooled to room temperature, succinimide was removed by
filtration, and the solid was washed with CCl4 (20 mL). The solution was
diluted with CH2Cl2 (100 mL) and washed successively with sat aq NaHCO3
(100 mL), sat aq Na2SO3 (100 mL), and brine (100 mL). The organic phase
was dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated under vacuum to give 7d.
1-Bromo-3,4-bis-bromomethyl-2,5-bis-dodecyloxybenzene (7g). A procedure
similar to that used in the synthesis of 7d employing NBS (17.0 g, 95.5
mmol) and compound 6g (26.3 g, 47.5 mmol) gave 33.2 g (46.7 mmol, 98%) of
7g as an off-white solid. mp 41-42 °C. IR (KBr) cm-1 1455, 1245; 1H NMR
(200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.87 (6H, t, J = 6.4 Hz), 1.25 (32H, s), 1.50 (4H, m),
1.82 (4H, m), 3.95 (2H, t, J = 6.4 Hz), 4.02 (2H, t, J = 6.6 Hz), 4.68
(2H, s), 4.70 (2H, s), 7.02 (1H, s); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.1,
22.7, 23.5, 23.7, 25.9, 26.0, 29.1, 29.2, 29.3, 29.5, 30.0, 31.9, 69.1,
74.2, 117.2, 118.4, 125.9, 132.7, 148.6, 153.8; HRMS (FAB+) calculated
for C32H5579Br2 81BrO2 (M+) 710.1734, found 710.1738 (+0.8 ppm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, selective for side chain bromination, IR heat lamp used
(250 W)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic crystal engineering with 1,4-piperazine-2,5-diones. 8. Synthesis,
crystal packing, and thermochemistry of piperazinediones derived from
2-amino-4,7-dialkoxyindan-2-carboxylic acids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
