$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.5. Bromination of sultones 2a-2d and 2g
(general procedure 4) Sultone 2a-2d or 2g (0.5 mmol) was dissolved in
CHCl3 (15 mL) in a two-necked flask equipped with a water condenser.
Bromine (0.75 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added, and the reaction mixture was
stirred at 65ºC bath temperature. HBr gas was removed from the reaction
mixture by a gentle argon flow. After 1 h, the reaction mixture was
cooled, and the volatiles were removed in vacuo. The residue was
dissolved in ethyl acetate, filtered through a 2-cm silica gel layer, and
the solvent was removed in vacuo. 4.5.1.
3-Bromo-4,6-diphenyl-[1,2]-oxathiine 2,2-dioxide (8a) 4.5.2.
3-Bromo-4,6-ditolyl-[1,2]-oxathiine 2,2-dioxide (8b) Yield: 97%. Pale
brown solid. m.p. 145-146ºC. Rf = 0.39 (pentane/ethyl acetate, 5:1). 1H
NMR: 2.41 (s, 3H), 2.43 (s, 3H), 6.44 (s, 1H), 7.25-7.32 (m, 4H), 7.38
(psd, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 7.63 (psd, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR: 21.41 (CH3),
21.52 (CH3), 104.97 (CH), 107.51 (C), 125.61 (2 CH), 127.43 (C), 128.04
(2 CH), 129.46 (2 CH), 129.77 (2 CH), 133.55 (C), 140.19 (C), 142.13 (C),
146.10 (C), 154.16 (C). MS (ESI): 391 [M+H]+; 408 [M+NH4]+. IR: 561, 588,
616, 643, 699, 741, 782, 813, 894, 958, 1011, 1030, 1099, 1123, 1175,
1192, 1273, 1312, 1369, 1409, 1502, 1540, 1753, 1606, 1623, 1684, 1734,
1916, 2857, 2920, 2956, 3033. Elemental analysis: calc. for C18H15BrO3S:
C 55.25, H 3.86, S 8.29; found: C 54.87, H 3.35, S 8.99.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple and practical one-step synthesis of new 1,3-diene δ-sultones from
terminal alkynes and some synthetic applications of these compounds
