$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
7,7-Dimethyl-4-bromo-6-trimethylsilyldithieno[2,3-b:4'3'-d]silole (6). To
a solution of 1 (5.49 g, 14.97 mmol) in chloroform (100 mL) was added NBS
(2.67 g, 4.97 mmol, 1.0 equiv) at ambient temperature for 5 h, and then
water (30 mL) was added to quench the reaction. The crude product was
extracted with chloroform (2 × 30 mL), and the organic layer was dried
over anhydrous MgSO4. After solvent was removed in vacuo, the residue was
purified by column chromatography with petroleum ether (60-90 °C) on
silica gel to yield 6. White solid, yield 5.42 g, 97.0%. Mp: 54-56 °C. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.91 (d, J= 4.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.68 (d, J= 4.8 Hz, 1
H), 0.53 (s, 6 H), δ 0.38 (s, 9 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 153.5,
149.9, 149.3, 147.3, 141.0, 134.8, 122.4, 105.3, 0.43, -0.9. IR (KBr):
2951.0, 2891.1 (C-H) cm-1. HRMS (TFMS ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for
C13H18BrS2Si2 372.95663, found 372.95697 [C13H1879BrS2Si2] and 374.9549
[C13H18 81BrS2Si2].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Dithieno[2,3-b:4',3'-d]siloles and Their Selective
Bromination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
