$DATUM Synthesis of
7,7-Dimethyl-4-bromo-2,6-di(trimethylsilyl)-dithieno[2,3-b:4'3'-d]silole
(10). To a solution of 2 (310.8 mg, 0.71 mmol) in chloroform (10 mL) was
added NBS (126.4 mg, 0.71 mmol, 1.0 equiv) at ambient temperature. After
about 4 h, the reaction was quenched with water (20 mL). The workup was
the same as that for the synthesis of 6. A white solid 10 (307.1 mg,
97.3%) was obtained by column chromatography on silica gel with petroleum
ether (60-90 °C) as eluent. From another reaction on the 90.0 mg scale of
2. Yield 87.4 mg, 95.6%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.99 (s, 1 H), 0.53
(s, 6 H), 0.39 (s, 9 H), 0.36 (s, 9 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
154.2, 151.9, 151.5, 149.3, 147.2, 147.0, 128.6, 105.2, 0.4, 0.0, -0.9.
IR (KBr): 2951.8, 2897.0 (C-H) cm-1. HRMS (TFMS ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd
for C16H26BrS2Si3 444.9967, found 444.9968 [C16H2679BrS2Si3] and 446.9947
[C16H2681BrS2Si3]. Formula weight: 445.66; Crystal system, space group:
Triclinic, P-1; Unit cell dimensions: a = 13.753(7) Å α= 98.458(11) °; b
= 14.627(7) Å β= 110.078(11) °; c = 14.647(12) Å γ= 117.942(7) °; Volume
= 2270(2) Å 3; Z, Calculated density: 4, 1.304 Mg/m3; Crystal size: 0.28
x 0.24 x 0.15 mm3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Dithieno[2,3-b:4',3'-d]siloles and Their Selective
Bromination
