$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.5. Bromination of sultones 2a-2d and 2g
(general procedure 4) Sultone 2a-2d or 2g (0.5 mmol) was dissolved in
CHCl3 (15 mL) in a two-necked flask equipped with a water condenser.
Bromine (0.75 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added, and the reaction mixture was
stirred at 65ºC bath temperature. HBr gas was removed from the reaction
mixture by a gentle argon flow. After 1 h, the reaction mixture was
cooled, and the volatiles were removed in vacuo. The residue was
dissolved in ethyl acetate, filtered through a 2-cm silica gel layer, and
the solvent was removed in vacuo. 4.5.1.
3-Bromo-4,6-diphenyl-[1,2]-oxathiine 2,2-dioxide (8a) 4.5.3.
3-Bromo-4,6-di(4-chlorphenyl)-[1,2]-oxathiine 2,2-dioxide (8c) Yield:
96%. Dark yellow solid. m.p. 149ºC. Rf = 0.32 (pentane/ethyl acetate,
5:1). 1H NMR: 6.42 (s, 1H), 7.40-7.50 (m, 6H), 7.67 (psd, J = 8.6 Hz,
2H). 13C NMR: 105.49 (CH), 109.38 (C), 126.90 (2 CH), 128.49 (C),129.26
(2 CH), 129.49 (4 CH), 134.31 (C), 136.29 (C), 137.94 (C), 144.78 (C),
153.30 (C). MS (ESI): 448/450/452 [M+NH4]+. IR: 684, 725, 755, 777, 845,
880, 946, 996, 1014, 1077, 1098, 1163, 1182, 1238, 1290, 1380, 1426,
1459, 1476, 1507, 1568, 1592, 1645, 1674, 1704, 1869, 2009, 2030, 2056,
2851, 2927, 2981, 3064, 3296. Elemental analysis: calc. for
C16H9BrCl2O3S: C 44.47, H 2.10, S 7.42; found: C 44.12, H 1.93, S 7.05.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple and practical one-step synthesis of new 1,3-diene δ-sultones from
terminal alkynes and some synthetic applications of these compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gaitzsch, Jens; Rogachev, Victor; Metz, Peter; Filimonov, Victor D.;
Zahel, Martin; Kataeva, Olga
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Sulfur Chemistry (2011), 32(1), 3-16

