$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of 2-bromo
allyl alcohol (2). Method A: A mixture of allyl alcohol derivative 1 (1.0
equiv) and pyridinium bromide perbromide (1.1 equiv) in
1,2-dichloroethane (0.1 M) was stirred at room temperature for 12-14h.
DBU (3.1 equiv) was added to the reaction mixture at 0 °C and the system
was then heated to 60 °C. The reaction was quenched with saturated
aqueous NH4Cl or 1 M aqueous HCl, and the reaction mixture was extracted
with dichloromethane or chloroform, concentrated in vacuo, and purified
by silica gel column chromatography to afford 2-bromo allyl alcohol 2.
Yield 95%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel One-Pot Method for Chemoselective Bromination and Sequential
Sonogashira Coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kutsumura, Noriki; Niwa, Kentaro; Saito, Takao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(15), 3316-3319

