$DATUM 4.5. Bromination of sultones 2a-2d and 2g (general procedure 4) Sultone
2a-2d or 2g (0.5 mmol) was dissolved in CHCl3 (15 mL) in a two-necked
flask equipped with a water condenser. Bromine (0.75 mmol, 1.5 equiv.)
was added, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 65ºC bath temperature.
HBr gas was removed from the reaction mixture by a gentle argon flow.
After 1 h, the reaction mixture was cooled, and the volatiles were
removed in vacuo. The residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate, filtered
through a 2-cm silica gel layer, and the solvent was removed in vacuo.
4.5.1. 3-Bromo-4,6-diphenyl-[1,2]-oxathiine 2,2-dioxide (8a) Yield: 95%.
Pale yellow solid. m.p. 144-145ºC. Rf = 0.34 (pentane/ethyl acetate,
5:1). 1H NMR: 6.50 (s, 1H), 7.44-7.55 (m, 8H), 7.73-7.76 (m, 2H). 13C
NMR: 105.62 (CH), 108.61 (C), 125.63 (2 CH), 128.03 (2 CH), 128.85 (2
CH), 129.06 (2 CH), 129.92 (CH), 130.12 (C), 131.47 (CH), 136.16 (C),
145.96 (C), 154.03 (C). MS (ESI): 380 [M+NH4]+. IR: 556, 609, 626, 676,
695, 753, 788, 804, 856, 888, 919, 957, 1014, 1038, 1072, 1100, 1187,
1236, 1287, 1372, 1419, 1447, 1473, 1485, 1493, 1621, 1654, 1697, 1733,
2922, 3004, 3031, 3087. Elemental analysis: calc. for C16H11BrO3S: C
52.91, H 3.05, S 8.83; found: C 52.82, H 2.80, S 9.01.
