$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM From cis-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(anthracen-10-yl). Method A. A carbon tetrachloride
(0.3 mL) solution of bromine (1.6 μL, 0.031 mmol) was added dropwise to a
stirred carbon tetrachloride solution (2 mL) of
cis-Pt(PEt3)2(Br)(anthracen-10-yl) (20.7 mg, 0.0300 mmol). The resulting
mixture was stirred for 15 min at room temperature and then the volatiles
were removed in vacuo. The solid residue was washed with cold hexane and
dried in vacuo to give 22 mg (95 %) of brown solid. 1H NMR (250 MHz,
C6D6): 9.41 (dd, J = 7.5 Hz, J = 1.75 Hz, 2H), 8.78 (dd, J = 7.25 Hz, J =
1.75 Hz 2H), 7.31-7.41 (m, 4H), 1.22-1.38 (m, 12H, CH2CH3), 0.62-0.74 (m,
18H, CH2CH3). 31P NMR (101 MHz, C6D6): 10.0 (s with satellites, J PtP =
2635 Hz). 13C{1H} NMR (62.9 MHz, C6D6): 152 (s), 138.6 (t with
satellites, J PC = 3.2 Hz, J PtC = 28.3 Hz), 136.3 (s with satellites, J
PtC = 96.4 Hz), 131.5 (s with satellites, J PtC = 60 Hz), 127.4 (s),
122.6 (s), 122.4 (s), 117.0 (s), 14.9 (t with satellites, J PC = 17.0 Hz,
J PtC = 69.5 Hz, PCH2CH3), 7.85 (s with satellites, J PtC = 22.3
Hz,PCH2CH3). 195Pt NMR (64.5 MHz, CDCl3): -2819.3 (t, J PtP = 2663 Hz).
Anal. Calcd (found) for C26H38Br2P2Pt: C, 40.69 (40.41); H, 4.99 (4.72).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
