$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1,2-Dibromo-1-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)alkanes
4a,b and 3-Bromo-1-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)alk-1-enes 4c,d; General
Procedure. A soln of 3a-d (10.8 mmol) in n-hexane or pentane (50 mL) was
stirred with Br2 (13 mmol) at r.t. for 12 h. Volatiles were removed and
the crude products were purified by chromatography (silica gel, n-hexane
or pentane) giving pure 4a-d (Schemes 4 and 5).
1,2-Dibromo-3-methyl-1-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)butane as a colorless
oil, yield 87%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.77 (d, J = 14.7 Hz, 1 H,
H2), 6.52 (d quint, JHH = 14.7 Hz, JHF = 6.0 Hz, 1 H, H1), 1.90 (s, 6 H,
CH3), 1.75-2.01 (m, 1 H, CH). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 144.1 (quint,
J = 6.7 Hz, C2), 138.6 (quint, J = 21.1 Hz, C1), 57.1 (CH), 32.7 (CH3).
19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 82.7 (9 lines, A-part), 64.0 (dd, J =
150.3, 6.0 Hz, B4-part). MS (EI): m/z (%) = 195 (100) [M - HBr - Br]+, 87
(45), 67 (25) [M - 2 HBr - SF5]+. Anal. Calcd for C5H9Br2F5S: C, 16.87;
H, 2.55; Br, 44.89; S, 9.01. Found: C, 16.90; H, 2.58; Br, 44.65; S,
8.98.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM the product structure and yield were corrected by the authors in the
erratum published in "Synthesis", 2011, (5), 827-828
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A mild and efficient synthesis of buta-1,3-dienes substituted with a
terminal pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl group
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ponomarenko, Maxim V.; Serguchev, Yurii A.; Roschenthaler, Gerd-Volker
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2010), (22), 3906-3912

