$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Dibromides 2a-l; General Procedure. A mixture
of the 1,3,5,7-tetramethyl-BODIPY 1 (0.2 mmol) and CuBr2 (0.5 mmol) in
anhyd MeCN (20 mL) was stirred under O2 atmosphere (balloon) at r.t. for
12 h. The residue obtained after the removal of the solvent by rotary
evaporation was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 40 mL), and the extracts were
washed with H2O (3 × 30 mL), dried (anhyd Na2SO4), and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The crude product was further purified using column
chromatography (EtOAc-petroleum ether) afforded compound.
2,6-Dibromo-4,4-difluoro-1,3,5,7-tetramethyl-8-phenyl-4-bora-3a,4a-diaza-s-indacene
(2a). Yield: 90.6 mg (94%); red solid. mp 229-231 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.38 (s, 6 H, CH3), 2.63 (s, 6 H, CH3), 7.26-7.28 (m, 2 H,
ArH), 7.54-7.55 (m, 3 H, ArH). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 152.9,
141.0, 139.6, 133.3, 129.3, 128.5, 128.4, 126.7, 110.7, 12.6. EI-MS: m/z
= 482 [M]+. Anal. Calcd for C19H17BBr2F2N2: C, 47.35; H, 3.56; N, 5.81.
Found: C, 47.39; H, 3.64; N, 5.76.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, oxygen (balloon) used, optimization study, optimized on
solvent,agent,temperature,stoichiometry, 2.5 equiv. of CuBr2 used,
product depends on stoichiometry and additives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient and convenient bromination of BODIPY derivatives with
copper(II) bromide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ye, Jia-Hai; Wang, Guangpu; Huang, Chengmei; Hu, Zhengjuan; Zhang,
Whenchao; Zhang, Yan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2012), 44(1), 104-110

