$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM α,α-Dichlorobenzyl Phenyl Sulfone (10a). Reaction of Benzyl Phenyl
Sulfone (10). (a) With C2Cl6 in Aqueous NaOH Under Phase-Transfer
Catalysis. Sulfone 10 was prepared as reported,7 A mixture of 10 (0.10 g,
0.4 mmol), C2Cl6 (0.31 g, 1.3 mmol), Aliquat 336 (0.01 g, 0.025 mmol), 2
mL of CH2Cl2, and 50% aq NaOH (0.65 mL, 12 mmol) was stirred for 12 h.
Water and CH2Cl2 were then added and the organic layer was separated,
dried, and concentrated as white crystals of 10a (0.12 g, 93% yield). mp
151-152 °C (lit.25 mp 151-152 °C). 1H NMR: δ 7.23-7.63 (m, 6 H), 7.75
(dd, J = 8 and 2 Hz, 4 H). 13C NMR: δ 99.61 (CCl2), 127.75, 128.24,
129.47, 130.91, 131.57, 131.97.132.38, 134.79.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Aliquat 336/catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unexpected differences in the α-halogenation and related reactivity of
sulfones with perhaloalkanes in KOH-t-BuOH
