$DATUM (S)-tert-Butyl
4-[(R)-1-acetoxy-3-bromoprop-2-ynyl]-2,2-dimethyloxazolidine-3-
carboxylate (12). To a solution of 11 (1.80 g, 3.97 mmol) in acetonitrile
(40 mL) were added NBS (848 mg, 4.76 mmol) and AgF (640 mg, 5.04 mmol) in
the dark. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 2 h
and then filtered through a pad of Celite. The filtrate was diluted with
EtOAc, washed with water, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 8:1) to give 12 (1.37 g, 92%) as a waxy
solid: (S)-tert-Butyl
4-[(R)-1-acetoxy-3-bromoprop-2-ynyl]-2,2-dimethyloxazolidine-3-
carboxylate (12), yield (1.37 g, 92%) [α]21 D - 89.8 (c 1.1, CHCl3); 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, mixture of rotamers) δ 1.45-1.53 (m, 15H), 2.09 (s,
3H), 3.99-4.20 (m, 3H), 5.81-5.83 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3,
rotamer 1/rotamer 2) δ 20.8/20.9, 23.1/24.4, 25.9/26.7, 28.2/28.3,
47.2/47.6, 59.5/59.7, 63.4/63.5, 64.4/63.9, 75.5, 80.7, 95.0/94.3,
151.4/152.3, 169.5; HRMS (CI) calcd for C15H23NO5Br ([M+H]+) 376.0821,
found 376.0762.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
