$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,6-(2-CHBr2C6H4)2-1-BrC6H3 (ii) To a solution of i (6.00 g, 17.8 mmol)
in 200 mL CCl4, N-bromosuccinimide (7.40 g, 41.6 mmol) and benzoyl
peroxide (50 mg) were added. The solution was heated to reflux for 6 h,
and another portion of N-bromosuccinimide (7.60 g, 42.7 mmol) and benzoyl
peroxide (50 mg) were added. After an additional 18 h reflux, the mixture
was cooled to RT, and the succinimide was removed by filtration; the
filtrate was washed with 5% NaSO3 (aq) (3 × 100 mL) and dried with
anhydrous MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated and the resulting solid was
washed with n-pentane to yield 10.7 g (92.0%) of ii as white solid.
(Chemical shifts of two isomers are reported without further assigning to
syn- or anti-) 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 6.41(s, CHBr2), 6.48 (s, CHBr2)
7.15, 7.19, 7.37-7.44 (m, 4H), 7.50-7.58 (m, 3H), 8.09, 8.11 (m, 2H). 13C
{1H} NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 38.8, 38.9 (CHBr2 of syn- or anti-), 124.9,
125.5 (Ar(C)-Br, syn- or anti-), 127.6, 127.7, 129.4, 129.8, 130.01,
130.05, 130.6, 130.8, 136.8, 137.0, 139.6, 139.7, 141.0. Elemental
analysis calcd for C20H13Br5 (652.84): C, 36.80; H, 2.01. Found: C,
36.61; H, 1.71.
