$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Silver-Catalyzed Iodination (Bromination) of
Diynes: Synthesis of diiododiyne 3a-I. A solution of dimethyl
dipropargylmalonate (2a) (208.3 mg, 1.0 mmol), N-iodosuccinimide (675.2
mg, 3.0 mmol), and AgNO3 (16.8 mg, 0.099 mmol) in dry DMF (6.0 mL) was
stirred for 3 h at room temperature in the dark. The reaction mixture was
then quenched with sat. Na2S2O3 (50 mL), and extracted with AcOEt (20 mL
× 3). The combined organic layer was washed with distilled water (40 mL ×
2) and brine (40 mL × 2), and dried with MgSO4. The solvent was removed
in vacuo and the residue was purified by flash column chromatography on
silica gel eluted with hexane/AcOEt (20:1 ~ 10:1) to give 3a-I (422.7 mg,
92%) as colorless solids colorless solids (mp. 94.9-95.1 °C): IR (CHCl3)
2253 (C=C), 1739 (C=O) cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.13 (s, 4 H),
3.76 (s, 6 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ -2.0, 25.2, 53.3, 56.8, 88.2,
168.6; MS (EI): m/z (%): 460 (8) [M+], 429 (20) [M+ - OCH3], 401 (15) [M+
- CO2Me], 301 (100) [M+ - HOCH3 - I]; EA calcd (%) for C11H10I2O4
(460.00): C 28.72, H 2.19; found: C 28.89, H 2.22.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Bicyclic p-Diiodobenzenes via Silver-Catalyzed Csp-H
Iodination and Ruthenium-Catalyzed Cycloaddition
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yamamoto, Yoshihiko; Hattori, Kozo; Nishiyama, Hisao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(25), 8336-8340

