$DATUM 91
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3-Bromomethyl-2-benzenesulfonylmethyl-1-methoxybenzene (4): To a solution
of 3 (0.276 g, 1 mmol) in carbon tetrachloride (25 ml) is added
N-bromosuccinimide (0.196 g, 1.1 mmol) and azobisisobutyronitrile (10 mg)
and the mixture is refluxed for 30 min. The mixture is refluxed by
illumination with a 200 W bulb. As soon as the reagent is converted to
succinic imide (20 min), the mixture is cooled, the imide is filtered off
and washed with carbon tetrachloride. Filtration and evaporation of the
filtrate gives a residue which is chromatographed on silica gel. Elution
with pentane/ether (6:4) affords the product. A sample is recrystallized
from chloroform/hexane for analytical purposes.
3-Bromomethyl-2-benzenesulfonylmethyl-1-methoxybenzene (4), yield: 0.324
(91%), crystalline product. m.p. 85-86°C. Molecular formula: C15H15BrO3S
(355.2). calc. C 50.76; H 4.23; S 9.00. found C 50.62; H 4.15; S 8.86.
1H-N.M.R. (CDCl3): δ = 3.19 (s, 3H); 4.73 (s, 2H); 4.81 (s, 2H);
6.52-7.67 ppm (m, 8H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of functionalized methoxybenzene derivatives via
regioselective homolytic monobromination of dimethylmethoxybenzenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ghera, E.; Plemenitas, A.; Ben-David, Y.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1984), (6), 504-6

