$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Silver-Catalyzed
Iodination (Bromination) of Diynes: Synthesis of diiododiyne 3a-I. A
solution of dimethyl dipropargylmalonate (2a) (208.3 mg, 1.0 mmol),
N-iodosuccinimide (675.2 mg, 3.0 mmol), and AgNO3 (16.8 mg, 0.099 mmol)
in dry DMF (6.0 mL) was stirred for 3 h at room temperature in the dark.
The reaction mixture was then quenched with sat. Na2S2O3 (50 mL), and
extracted with AcOEt (20 mL × 3). The combined organic layer was washed
with distilled water (40 mL × 2) and brine (40 mL × 2), and dried with
MgSO4. The solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue was purified by
flash column chromatography on silica gel eluted with hexane/AcOEt (20:1
~ 10:1) to give 3a-I (422.7 mg, 92%) as colorless solids 15: mp.
109.0-109.5 °C; IR (CHCl3) 1740 (CO2Me) cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
3.01 (s, 4 H), 3.09 (s, 4 H), 3.74 (s, 6 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
-1.6, 23.7, 25.2, 53.3, 56.5, 68.0, 72.1, 88.0, 168.4; MS (EI): m/z (%):
667 (6) [M+], 607 (10) [M+ - H – CO2Me], 546 (94) [M+ - 3H – 2CO2Me], 487
(78) [M+ - 3H – 3CO2Me], 419 (100) [M+ - 3H – 2CO2Me - I]; EA calcd (%)
for C22H20I2O8 (666.20): C 39.66, H 3.03; found: C 39.78, H 3.10.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Bicyclic p-Diiodobenzenes via Silver-Catalyzed Csp-H
Iodination and Ruthenium-Catalyzed Cycloaddition
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
