$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction of 2-Alkylidenetetrahydrofurans or
Furans with NBS; General Procedure To a CCl4 solution (5 mL/mmol) of
2-alkylidenetetrahydrofuran (2 or 9) or furan (10) (1 equiv) was added
NBS (1.1-1.8 equiv, see Table 1) at 20 °C. The reaction mixture was
heated and stirred under reflux for 3 h, allowed to cool to ambient
temperature, and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The residue was
purified by chromatography (n-hexane-EtOAc) to give the brominated
2-alkylidenetetrahydrofuran (3, 4, 5, or 6) or furan (11). Ethyl
[3-Bromo-3-butyldihydrofuran-2(3H)-ylidene]acetate (3e) Ethyl
[3-butyldihydrofuran-2(3H)-ylidene]acetate (2e; 0.127 g, 0.6 mmol) and
NBS (0.139 g, 0.78 mmol) in CCl4 (15 mL) gave 3e after chromatography
(n-hexane-EtOAc, 50:1→ 1:1). Yield: 0.160 g (91%); yellowish oil. IR
(neat): 2958 (s), 2932 (s), 2869 (m), 1717 (s), 1652 (s), 1463 (m), 1437
(m), 1388 (m), 1329 (m), 1298 (m), 1272 (m), 1206 (s), 1181 (s), 1156
(s), 1116 (m), 1102 (m), 1951 (s), 1021 (m), 964 (w), 807 (m) cm-1. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 0.96 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3 H, CH3), 1.28 (t, J =
7.2 Hz, 3 H, OCH2CH3), 1.32-1.46 (m, 3 H, 2 × CH2), 1.60- 1.74 (m, 1 H,
CH2), 1.77-1.87 (m, 1 H, CH2), 2.05-2.16 (m, 1 H, CH2), 2.20-2.30 (m, 1
H, CH2), 2.44 (dd, J = 14.1, 4.8 Hz, 1 H, CH2), 4.17 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H,
OCH2CH3), 4.49-4.61 (m, 2 H, OCH2), 5.10 (s, 1 H, CH=C). 13C NMR (CDCl3,
75 MHz): δ = 13.8 (CH3), 22.5, 28.2, 39.9, 40.4 (CH2), 59.7 (C-5), 67.9
(CBr), 71.2 (OCH2), 88.1 (CH=CO), 16.2 (O=CO), 172.5 (OC=CH). MS (EI, 70
eV): m/z (%) = 292 (M+ [81Br], 4), 290 (M+ [79Br], 4), 278 (5), 276 (5),
247 (24), 245 (23), 236 (12), 234 (12), 222 (15), 220 (16), 211 (22), 197
(35), 183 (10), 181 (9), 179 (9), 169 (83), 167 (17), 165 (47), 155
(100), 137 (31), 127 (11), 123 (71), 121 (6), 119 (11), 112 (28), 110
(12), 108 (17), 98 (24), 81 (22), 70 (64).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of functionalized furans based on a '[3+2]
cyclization/bromination/elimination' strategy
