$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Brominated Ga-corrole, Ga(pyr)(tpfc-Br8), was synthesized as follows:
initially adding bromine (200 μL, 1.6 mmol) to a benzene solution (3 mL)
of Ga(pyr)(tpfc) (30 mg, 32 μmol), and after an overnight stirring, the
solvent was evaporated by a stream of N2. The residue was passed through
a column of silica with CH2Cl2/pyridine 100:1. After recrystallization
from n-hexane/CH2Cl2. Ga(pyr)(tpfc-Br8), yield 45 mg, 29 μmol, 90%. 19F
NMR (188 MHz, CD3OD, δ): -139.9 (dd, 3J(F,F) = 23.9, 4J = 8.3 Hz, 2F;
ortho-F), -140.2 (dd, 3J(F,F) = 23.9, 4J = 7.7 Hz, 4F; ortho- F), -156.1
(t, 3J(F,F) = 20.3 Hz, 2F; para-F), -156.2 (t, 3J(F,F) = 19.4 Hz, 1F;
para-F), -166.6 (m, 4F; meta-F), -167.00 (m, 2F; meta-F). UV/vis (CH2Cl2,
nm, ε x 10-3 M-1 cm-1): 436 (103.5), 586 (11.0), 612 (8.8). MS (TOF FD)
m/z (%) 1574 (100%) [M], 1494 [M - pyridine] (15%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Photoexcited triplet state properties of brominated and nonbrominated
Ga(III)-corroles as studied by time-resolved electron paramagnetic
resonance
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wagnert, Linn; Rubin, Roy; Berg, Alexander; Mahammed, Atif; Gross, Zeev;
Levanon, Haim
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Physical Chemistry B (2010), 114(45), 14303-14308

