$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B: A mixture of allyl alcohol
derivative 1 (1.0 equiv), pyridinium bromide perbromide (1.1 equiv), and
potassium carbonate (1.1 equiv) in 1,2-dichloroethane (0.1 M) was stirred
at room temperature for 12-14h. DBU (1.1 equiv) was added to the reaction
mixture at 0 °C and the system was then heated to 60 °C. The reaction was
quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl or 1 M aqueous HCl, and the
reaction mixture was extracted with dichloromethane or chloroform,
concentrated in vacuo, and purified by silica gel column chromatography.
Yield 90%
