$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(5-(Benzyloxy)penta-1,3-diynyl)triisopropylsilane (8). To a degassed
solution of 7 (1.02 g, 4.53 mmol), (triisopropylsilyl)acetylene (1.20 mL,
5.40 mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (32 mg, 0.046 mmol) and CuI (8.5 mg, 0.045 mmol)
in THF (15 mL) was added diisopropylamine (1.30 mL, 9.28 mmol). The
reaction mixture was stirred for 2 h at room temperature and then
quenched with saturated NH4Cl solution. It was diluted with ether, washed
with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
resulting residue was purified by flash silica gel column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc, 50:1) to give TIPS-diyne 8 (1.30 g, 88%) as a yellow oil.
Methyl 10-bromodec-9-ynoate (19).8a Following the same procedure as for
7, from 18(495 mg, 1.95 mmol) in acetone (20 mL), N-bromosuccinimide (406
mg, 2.28 mmol), and AgNO3 (34 mg, 0.20 mmol), after a reaction time of 2
h, bromo-acetylene 19 (458 mg, 90%) was obtained as a colorless oil. 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.26-1.40 (m, 6H), 1.43-1.52 (m, 2H), 1.54-1.64
(m, 2H), 2.16 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 2.27 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 3.63 (s,
3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 19.5, 24.8, 28.1, 28.5, 28.6, 28.9, 33.9,
37.5, 51.3, 80.2, 174.1; IR (CHCl3) νmax 2934.0, 2858.8, 1738.0, 1458.3,
1435.2, 1197.7, 1170.1(cm-1); MS (CI) m/z (rel int) 261 ([M+1]+, 21);
HRMS (CI) calcd for C11H18O2Br ([M+1]+) 261.0490, found 261.0485.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New, Iterative Strategy for the Synthesis of Unsymmetrical Polyynes:
Application to the Total Synthesis of 15,16-Dihydrominquartynoic Acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kim, Sanghee; Kim, Shinae; Lee, Taeho; Ko, Hyojin; Kim, Deukjoon
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2004), 6(20), 3601-3604

