$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
2-Alkyl-1-(bromoethynyl)-cyclohexanol (10): To a solution of 9a-e (1.3
mmol), N-bromosuccinimide (1.5 mmol) and AgNO3 (0.5 mmol) in acetone (10
mL) were added, and the resulting solution was stirred in darkness for 2
h at room temperature. Acetone was evaporated under reduced pressure, and
the solids were removed by filtration through a Celite pad (washing with
ether). The combined organic phase were concentrated and subjected to
purification by column chromatography using hexane:EtOAc 9:1.
(1S,2S)-1-(Bromoethynyl)-2-((methoxymethoxy)methyl)cyclohexanol 10c as a
yellow liquid, yield 327 mg, 90%. TLC (Hexane: EtOAc 9:1): Rf = 0.39 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ= 1.33-2.07 (m, 9H), 3.41(s, 3H), 3.59 (dd, 1H, J =
2.4, 9.6 Hz), 4.24 (dd, 1H, J = 3.3, 9.6 Hz), 4.65 (dd, 2H, J = 6.6, 13.2
Hz). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ= 20.61, 24.67, 25.51, 39.17, 43.23, 45.09,
55.39, 70.66, 70.87, 84.39, 96.51. HRMS m/z 259.0104, 261.0123[M - OH]+,
calculated 259.0334, 261.0314 [M - OH]+.
