$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure 2: To a flask were added phthalide (6 mmol), NBS (7.2
mmol), and AIBN (0.6 mmol) under an argon atmo-sphere. The mixture was
well mixed with stirring for 2 min. Then the mixture was heated at 60 °C
until the starting phthalide was consumed completely. After one hour,
diethyl ether (15 mL) was added to the mixture, and the obtained mixture
was filtered to re-move succinimide. The filtrate was evaporated and the
residue was chromatographed on silica gel (eluent: hexane-ethyl acetate =
1:1) to give 3-bromophthalide. Yield 89%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, regioselective, Wohl-Ziegler reaction, reaction
alternately run with AIBN as catalyst with comparable yield or in
[bmim]PF6 solvent with lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Environmentally-friendly Wohl-Ziegler bromination: Ionic-liquid reaction
and solvent-free reaction
