$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of Cyclohexene with
N,N'-Dibromo-N,N'-1,2-ethylene bis(2,5-Dimethyl Benzenesulfonamide). A
Typical Procedure In a 50 mL round-bottomed flask 5.41 g (0.0098 mol) of
N-bromo-sulfonamide, 30 mL of carbon tetrachloride, 1.61 g (0.0196 mol)
of redistilled cyclohexene and 0.05 g of benzoyl peroxide is placed. The
flask is equipped with a condenser and the reaction mixture allowed to
stand at room temperature. After a short induction period the reaction
mixture becomes warm and light, colourless sulfonamide(crystals) begin to
precipitate. The flask was cold in ice-water. After the reaction the
sulfonamide was filtered under suction and. washed with 10 mL of cold
carbon tetrachloride. Distil the filterate on a boiling water bath, first
of all the carbon tetrachloride was removed (b.p. 77°C), then, unreacted
cyclohexene (b.p. 83°C). The residue was distilled (b.p. 66-67°C/20mm)
with 60% yield. This compound was identified by T.L.C, IR, NMR
spectroscopies and elemental analysis. Ethyl 4-Bromobut-2-enoate The
residue was distilled (b.p. 94-95°C/12mm) with 89% yield. This compound
was identified by T.L.C, IR, NMR spectroscopies and elemental analysis
b.p. 94-95°C/12mm; IR (KBr pellets) 3050, 2950, 1750, 1430, 1280, 1100,
1000, 900, 850cm-1; 1H-NMR (CDCl3): δ = 1.3 (t, 3H), δ = 4.1 (m, 4H), δ =
6 (d, 1H), δ = 7 (m, 1H); 13C-NMR: δ = 164.351, 128.483, 119.315, 64.232,
30.16. Found: C, 31.21; H, 4.61%. Calcd. for C6H9BrO2: C, 31.11; H,
4.70%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, global reaction time 10h
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Bromination of organic allylic compounds by using
N,N'-dibromo-N,N'-1,2-ethane diyl bis(2,5-dimethyl benzene sulfonyl)amine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Khazaei, Ardeshir; Vaghei, Ramin Ghorbani; Karkhanei, Ebrahim
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2002), 32(14), 2107-2113

